   This is the number a reader needs before choosing an exhaustiveness. A rung's verdict
   depends on how many poses get inspected: extra sampling finds poses that Vina's own
   scoring function then fails to promote to rank 1, so a step can be worth nothing at
   rank-1 and clearly worth paying for a few ranks down.

   This section is a YIELD statement only. It carries no cost, so it stands whether or
   not a segment's cost delta was measurable.

8. KNEE

   Pre-registered cell: triple at oracle (all poses).
   Knee = exhaustiveness 92 — the largest rung whose incoming marginal-return
   interval excludes zero, in that cell.

   Claimed in ONE cell only, fixed before looking. Taking the largest rung whose
   interval clears zero across many gate x depth cells is a maximum over a family of
   uncorrected intervals and places a knee at the top rung far more often than its
   nominal rate. Every other cell in this report is descriptive.

   The knee is bounded above by the largest arm in the ladder. 'Exhaustiveness beyond
   128 does not help' is NOT supported by anything here; only 'no benefit was
   detectable between the top two rungs at this depth' is.

